Spoilers on how to blow away high level nasties in Sporkhack follow.
















So my rogue sits on the one spot the Big B is going to want to come to
and here's what happens to him.

You engrave in the floor with the blessed rustproof +2 Magicbane
(weapon in hand).
What do you want to engrave in the floor here?  Elbereth
Baalzebub bites!  Baalzebub points at you, then curses.
The magic-absorbing blade cancels Baalzebub!  Baalzebub resists!
Baalzebub is stunned.  Baalzebub bites!  Baalzebub points at you, then
curses.
You hit Baalzebub!  Baalzebub turns to flee!  Baalzebub bites!
Baalzebub points all around, then curses.
You strike Baalzebub from behind!  Baalzebub bites!
Baalzebub points at you, then curses.
You strike Baalzebub from behind!  The magic-absorbing blade scares
Baalzebub!
Baalzebub resists!  Baalzebub is stunned.
You strike Baalzebub from behind!  The magic-absorbing blade scares
Baalzebub!
Baalzebub resists!  Baalzebub is stunned.
Baalzebub reads a scroll of create monster!
You strike Baalzebub from behind!  The magic-absorbing blade stuns
Baalzebub!
Baalzebub bites!  Baalzebub points all around, then curses.
You strike Baalzebub from behind!  You kill Baalzebub!

He never once moved more than arm's reach from my rogue and at the end
of this battle my rogue was at full hit points.  (With a few eroded
armor bits from the short walk on the level above.)

This is Sporkhack so at least he makes a half hearted attempt to fight
back, but it's still an easy slaughter.  (Note the combination of the
multiple E-word checks, Magicbane's status inflictions and the rogue's
backstab bonus.)

When they're scared these high level foes need to run and get out of
line of sight please so they can heal up and cast summon nasties.

